# Deeply nested function calls no longer limited by MAX_CONTINUATION_STACK
# With T-908, the continuation stack depth limit has been removed.
# This Y-combinator style recursive function now succeeds (limited only by OS memory).
# Note: This is NOT tail-recursive, so each call adds continuation frames.
# The test uses a small depth (100) to avoid excessive runtime.
[f: [fn [let self n] [if [= n 0] 0 [+ 1 [call self self [- n 1]]]]]
 result: [call f f 100]]
=== out
Int(100)
